TASK A1 – DECOMPOSE THE PROGRAM INTO FUNCTIONS (7 Marks)
A1.1 – Identify the Functions (2 Marks)
Aim: To divide the Blood Bank Management System into smaller functions so that the program is modular, easy to maintain, test and reuse.
Functions of the Blood Bank System
Function Purpose
registerDonor() Registers a new donor and stores donor details.
checkEligibility() Checks whether a donor is eligible for donation.
findDonors() Finds eligible donors belonging to a required blood group.
findYoungestEligible() Finds the youngest eligible donor.
updateStock() Updates the blood stock after donation or issue.
saveDonors() Saves donor details into a file.
loadDonors() Loads donor details from a file.
saveStock() Stores blood stock information into a file.
loadStock() Reads blood stock information from a file.
displayDonors() Displays donor details.

